            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="0762" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-29T09:00:00+02:35">September 29,
                            1935—9 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 29—6:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. I am reliably informed that unless Ethiopia receives assurances from the
                    League or the Powers within a day or two that Italy will be restrained by force
                    if necessary, the Emperor will order a general mobilization which may have the
                    gravest consequences but for which he will decline all responsibility.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
